---
import Layout from '~/layouts/Layout.astro';

const updated = '17 September 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Support | Canopy"
  description="How to reach Canopy: one monitored address, what to include, and what happens next."
>
  <div class="legal">
    <div class="shell legal__inner">
      <p class="section-kicker">Support</p>
      <h1>Getting help</h1>
      <p class="legal__lead">
        One address reaches us:
        <a href="mailto:hello@canopy.ag">hello@canopy.ag</a>. It is monitored by the team
        that builds the product, not a queue that routes elsewhere.
      </p>
      <p class="legal__meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <h2>What to expect</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to reply within one working day. Canopy is a small team, so an answer comes
        from someone who can act on it. If something is broken and it is stopping work in
        your operation, say so in the subject line and we will treat it that way.
      </p>

      <h2>What helps us help you</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your organization, and the site or zone if the problem is specific to one.</li>
        <li>What you expected to happen, and what happened instead.</li>
        <li>Roughly when it happened, so we can find it in the logs.</li>
        <li>A screenshot, if it is something you can see.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        None of it is required. A short message beats no message.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting a security issue</h2>
      <p>
        Send it to <a href="mailto:hello@canopy.ag">hello@canopy.ag</a> with "security" in
        the subject. Please give us a reasonable chance to fix it before disclosing it
        publicly, and we will keep you informed while we do.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy requests</h2>
      <p>
        Requests for a copy of your information, a correction, or deletion go to the same
        address. What we hold and how it is handled is described in our
        <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Not a customer yet</h2>
      <p>
        If you are trying to work out whether Canopy fits your operation, the same address
        works, or you can <a href="/">request a demo</a> from the home page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 8rem 0 6rem;
  }
  .legal__inner {
    max-width: 46rem;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
  }
  .legal p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.62);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal__lead {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75) !important;
  }
  .legal__meta {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35) !important;
    margin-bottom: 2rem !important;
  }
  .legal a {
    color: #22c55e;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .legal a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .legal strong {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
  }
  .legal ul {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.62);
    line-height: 1.7;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>
